  "text_input": "Patient was apparently normal 2 days back when he developed complaints of stiffness of bilateral upper and lower limbs along with involuntary movements of bilateral upper and lower limbs. The episode lasted for about 2 minutes. It was associated with post-ictal confusion, frothing of saliva, teeth and tongue biting. Patient could hear but was not able to respond during the episode. There was up-rolling of eyes during the episode. No complaints of headache or blurring of vision. Post-ictal confusion lasted for about 1 minute after the episode.\nNo history of weakness of limbs or speech disturbance. No history of involuntary urination or diarrhea. No history of fever, vomiting, or altered sensorium. No history of trauma",
